    "doi": null,
    "abstract": "The oceans cover over two-thirds of the Earth\u2019s surface.&#13;\\nThey play a vital role in global biogeochemical cycles,&#13;\\ncontribute enormously to the planet\u2019s biodiversity and&#13;\\nprovide a livelihood for millions of people. (...)",
    "field": "Ocean acidification",
    "problem": "This report addresses the problem that increasing atmospheric CO\u2082 is causing ocean acidification, but the complex and significant impacts of this rapid chemical change on marine organisms, calcification processes, and entire ecosystems are poorly understood and represent a recently recognized environmental threat requiring a scientific overview.",
    "method": "To mitigate ocean acidification, this report concludes that reducing global carbon dioxide emissions to the atmosphere is the only practical way to minimize the risk of large-scale and long-term changes to the oceans, as other engineering approaches are considered unproven and impractical.",
    "task": "The task is to provide a concise overview of the scientific knowledge of ocean acidification due to increasing atmospheric carbon dioxide and assess its likely impacts on marine organisms, ecosystems, and socio-economic systems.",
